  "title": "Chapter 9 – Hand Tools and Their Uses",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "jr3fh0s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Hand tools are classified by function into striking, holding, driving, cutting, and measuring tools.",
        "Hammers are designated by their weight and peen shape (ball-peen, cross-peen, straight-peen).",
        "Spanners and pliers provide mechanical advantage for gripping, turning, and cutting fasteners or wires.",
        "Files remove thin layers of metal and are specified by length, grade, cut, and shape.",
        "Hacksaws and cold chisels serve as primary manual cutting tools for metals and structural shapes."
      ],
      "id": "6tj9j4u"
    },
