    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ball-peen hammers are the standard choice in fitting shops for general bench work and riveting.",
        "Hacksaw blade pitch selection depends on material thickness: coarse pitch (1.8 mm) for soft metals, fine pitch (0.8 mm) for thin tubes/conduits.",
        "Chisel point angle for mild steel is standard at 60 degrees.",
        "Files are made of High Carbon Steel; the 'Bastard' file is a grade of file, not a cut type."
      ],
